 Cant' read in the dark, LOL but makes me feel at home and I can go by myself and watch old movies or tv shows have special nights there. Pool table, love seat...the list goes on...slot machines. Bathrooms are clean. Then you go to the back and there is a pretty good sized Vietnamese restaurant with great Pho and some vegan items and a stage for things like Comedy Catastrophe. I've been a couple times and each time w..."},{"business_id":"0JlxuzzDo1Sv89S9ApI9Ng","review_id":"1R6Pds2qMkIwduMw1jwc3A","date":"2013-04-01T17:33:01","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9237555861473083,"text_excerpt":"The Vietnamese kitchen in the back is yummy, and the drinks are reasonably priced. They always have a good wine special going, with glasses being mostly $5, sometimes $6. They usually have a cocktail special as well, but I pretty much always get beer. Whenever I can't find a friend with HBO, this is where I go to get my True Blood and Game of Thrones fix. Be warned, it gets pretty crowded on these nights, so show up an hour in advance to grab a good seat and nom on some pho. I love this place. What's not to love?"},{"business_id":"0JlxuzzDo1Sv89S9ApI9Ng","review_id":"pfiyLYjZQ_zpz8ErMNsnXQ","date":"2011-05-30T13:49:06","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9163602590560913,"text_excerpt":"came here a few weeks ago to eat, drink, and watch \"Tremé.\" sat on the restaurant side and got there way early, which was necessary it turns out because the place fills up for the show. for as busy as it is, with the drinking and the order taking though, it is also a very quiet, respectful crowd. had the bun, some apps, and several pimm's cups. certainly not game-changing food, but also definitely the best vietnamese i've had on the east bank while watching \"Tremé.\" that's gotta count for something, right?"}],"visual":[{"business_id":"0JlxuzzDo1Sv89S9ApI9Ng","photo_id":"xcXsYAZ3QPMrA4z_ESFbdw","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/xcXsYAZ3QPMrA4z_ESFbdw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0